<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιφέρω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set against,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Erx.</u>
				395b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πόλεμον ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.438
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Damag.
			</span></i>): used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in 
				Med.
			 or 
				Pass.
			, <i>set oneself against, fight against</i> another, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντεφέροντο μάχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.701
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργαλέος γὰρ Ὀλύμπιος
				ἀντιφέρεσθαι</span> hard <i>to oppose,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1.589
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.238
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μένος ἀ. τινί</span>
			<i>match oneself with</i> another in strength, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.482
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς Ὁμηρείοις ἀντιφέροιτο λόγοις;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.625
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be borne in a contrary direction to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ οὐρανῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					291b2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				215a30
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ παντὶ τὴν φοράν</span>
			Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.134
			</span></i> H.</div>
